{
  "version": 1,
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Lab 5 — ProtectWeatherConfig Rule"
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "kind": 1,
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": "# Lab 5 — `ProtectWeatherConfig` Rule\n\nRight now, any authenticated MQTT user can publish to `config/heat_limit_c` and silence or falsify heat alerts. In this lab, you will deploy a **Rule** (`DEFINE RULE`) that restricts publishing under `config/#` to `root` only.\n\n### How `ProtectWeatherConfig` works\n- **`WITH PRIORITY 1`:** Evaluated before the default `AllowAll` rule (which has priority `100` — lower number runs first).\n- **`FOR PublishToBroker`:** Applies only when a client publishes a message to the broker.\n- **`IF USER IS NOT \"root\" AND TOPIC MATCHES \"config/#\" THEN DENY`:** Blocks any non-`root` user from publishing to `config/` or any sub-topic under it.\n\n> **Licence note:** Custom RBAC rules require an **event licence** (Trial / Growth / Enterprise). Activate your `CFLX-…` code in **`root` (top right) → Broker Settings → License → Activation code** before clicking **▷**. If you are on **Community Edition**, you can read through this cell and move straight to **`06-panel.lotnb`**."
    },
    {
      "kind": 2,
      "language": "lot",
      "value": "DEFINE RULE ProtectWeatherConfig WITH PRIORITY 1 FOR PublishToBroker\n    IF USER IS NOT \"root\" AND TOPIC MATCHES \"config/#\" THEN\n        DENY\n    ELSE\n        ALLOW\n"
    },
    {
      "kind": 1,
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": "### Test it with a non-root user (`bob`)\n\n1. Click **`root` (top right) → Broker Settings → Users & Permissions → Add User** and create user **`bob`** (any password, **Client** role).\n2. Click **▷** on the cell above to deploy `ProtectWeatherConfig`.\n3. Click **`root` (top right) → Switch Broker** and connect as **`bob`** (`broker:1883`).\n   *(Because `bob` is not an admin, the HUB opens in limited mode with **Data Viewer**.)*\n4. In **Data Viewer → Publish**, try publishing `5` (Retain **ON**) to `config/heat_limit_c`. The broker silently drops unauthorized publishes.\n5. Click **`bob` (top right) → Switch Broker**, select your saved **`root` @ `broker:1883`** session, and check `config/heat_limit_c` in **Data Viewer** — it is still **`30`**!\n\n> **Updating a Rule later:** Unlike Actions and Models, re-deploying a Rule with the same name returns `Rule already exists`. Run `-removeRule ProtectWeatherConfig` in **Command Console** before deploying an updated version.\n\n**Next up:** Open **`06-panel.lotnb`** to build the live operator dashboard!"
    }
  ]
}
